            ("p", "Most companies are stuck in the same place right now. A handful of curious employees are using AI tools on their own, building clever prompts, saving themselves an hour here and there, and quietly becoming the \"AI person\" on their team. Meanwhile, the organization as a whole has no shared capability at all. If that employee leaves, the knowledge leaves with them. If a new hire joins, they start from zero. This is what I call novice, individual AI enablement, and it's where the vast majority of companies sit today."),
